From 4ad78d39740b931a7bf73bbd5ccf2c29b7fc4d0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex native diagnostic <noreply@native-diagnostic.invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 06:18:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mediatek: admit capability after START readiness

START readiness transitions the INIT transaction from START_READY to
INIT_IDLE. The capability gate still required START_READY, so the
first query returned -EIO before any HIF access. Accept only the
post-readiness idle phase while retaining the firmware-ready and
one-attempt guards.

This is an internal diagnostic patch, not an upstream submission.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/hif.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/hif.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/hif.c
index 6f18599..7c58127 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/hif.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/hif.c
@@ -335,7 +335,7 @@ int mt6797_hif_query_capability(struct mt6797_hif *hif, unsigned int sequence,
 		return -EBUSY;
 	trace->stage = MT6797_CAP_ENTER;
 	if (!hif->firmware_ready || hif->capability_attempted ||
-	    hif->transaction->phase != MT6797_START_READY) {
+	    hif->transaction->phase != MT6797_INIT_IDLE) {
 		error = -EIO;
 		goto unlock;
 	}
